GST Reconciliation Toolkit

An open-source GST reconciliation tool built using Python to simplify the process of comparing GSTR-2B data with purchase register data.

About the Project

GST Reconciliation Toolkit is designed to help businesses, accountants, and tax professionals reconcile their purchase records with GSTR-2B data. The tool aims to identify invoice mismatches, missing entries, and ITC differences, making GST reconciliation faster and more efficient.

Key Features

- Compare GSTR-2B with Purchase Register.
- Identify matched and mismatched invoices.
- Detect missing purchase invoices.
- Verify GSTIN, invoice number, taxable value, and tax amounts.
- Identify differences in Input Tax Credit (ITC).
- Generate detailed reconciliation reports in Excel.
- Display reconciliation results through a simple dashboard.

Technology Stack

- Python
- Streamlit
- Pandas
- OpenPyXL

Project Goals

- Simplify the GST reconciliation process.
- Reduce manual Excel work.
- Improve accuracy in ITC reconciliation.
- Save time for accountants and tax professionals.
- Provide a simple and user-friendly tool.

Project Status

Currently under development. Features will be added and improved progressively.

